yond timeout\"\n   458→    expected:\n   459→      postcondition: test fails with clear timeout message, not a hang\n   460→    traces:\n   461→      - prd001-testutils R2.3\n   462→\n   463→  - name: env_default_lc_all\n   464→    description: RunDiffTests sets LC_ALL=C by default when DiffTest.Env is nil.\n   465→    inputs:\n   466→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: nil\"\n   467→      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n   468→    expected:\n   469→      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=C\"\n   470→    traces:\n   471→      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n   472→\n   473→  - name: env_override_lc_all\n   474→    description: DiffTest.Env overrides the LC_ALL=C default.\n   475→    inputs:\n   476→      function: 'testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"}'\n   477→      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n   478→    expected:\n   479→      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"\n   480→    traces:\n   481→      - prd001-testutils R1.3\n   482→      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n   483→\n   484→  - name: workdir_default_tempdir\n   485→    description: WorkDir defaults to t.TempDir() when empty.\n   486→    inputs:\n   487→      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with WorkDir: \\\"\\\"\"\n   488→      setup: \"mock binary prints working directory\"\n   489→    expected:\n   490→      postcondition: both binaries run in a temporary directory\n   491→    traces:\n   492→      - prd001-testutils R2.5\n   493→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1b79863-0b40-4bd6-8be0-3edd1f9e69f7","uuid":"a0cb4455-cfe1-4cd6-b8e1-b52ec64e0ba8","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/86/docs/specs/test-suites/test-rel00.0.yaml","content":"id: test-rel00.0\ntitle: \"Test Suite: rel00.0 — build lifecycle, cmd/version, pkg/format, pkg/sys, and pkg/testutils\"\nrelease: rel00.0\n\ntraces:\n  - rel00.0-uc001-magefiles\n  - prd011-magefiles R1\n  - prd011-magefiles R2\n  - prd011-magefiles R3\n  - prd011-magefiles R4\n  - rel00.0-uc002-format\n  - prd003-format R1\n  - prd003-format R2\n  - prd003-format R3\n  - rel00.0-uc003-sys\n  - prd002-sys R1\n  - prd002-sys R2\n  - prd002-sys R3\n  - prd002-sys R4\n  - rel00.0-uc004-testutils\n  - prd001-testutils R1\n  - prd001-testutils R2\n  - prd001-testutils R3\n  - prd001-testutils R4\n  - prd001-testutils R5\n\npreconditions:\n  - A git repository with at least one tag matching v[0-9]*.\n  - golangci-lint is installed and on PATH.\n  - mage is installed and on PATH.\n  - configuration.yaml exists at the project root with project.binary_dir set to bin.\n\ntest_cases:\n  # --- uc001-magefiles: build lifecycle and version ---\n\n  - name: build_produces_version_binary\n    description: mage build compiles cmd/version to bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage build\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      postcondition: bin/version exists and is executable\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R2.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R2.4\n\n  - name: version_prints_tag\n    description: bin/version prints the latest version tag and exits 0.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout_pattern: \"v[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\\\.[0-9]+\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.3\n\n  - name: version_flag_identical\n    description: bin/version --version produces the same output as bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version --version\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_v_flag_identical\n    description: bin/version -v produces the same output as bin/version.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version -v\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: same as bin/version with no arguments\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_unknown_flag\n    description: bin/version --bogus prints usage to stderr and exits 2.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"bin/version --bogus\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 2\n      stdout: \"\"\n      stderr_contains: \"usage\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.4\n\n  - name: version_dev_build\n    description: A build without ldflags prints \"dev\".\n    inputs:\n      command: \"go build -o /tmp/version-dev ./cmd/version && /tmp/version-dev\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      stdout: \"dev\\n\"\n      stderr: \"\"\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R1.2\n\n  - name: lint_passes\n    description: mage lint runs golangci-lint with no warnings.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage lint\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R3.1\n      - prd011-magefiles R3.2\n\n  - name: clean_removes_bin\n    description: mage clean removes the bin/ directory.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage build && mage clean\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n      postcondition: bin/ does not exist\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n\n  - name: clean_idempotent\n    description: mage clean succeeds when bin/ does not exist.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"mage clean && mage clean\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd011-magefiles R4.1\n\n  # --- uc002-format: pkg/format output formatting ---\n\n  - name: columns_20_entries_80_width\n    description: Columns distributes 20 filenames into a grid fitting 80 columns.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Columns(entries, 80)\"\n      entries: 20 filenames of varying lengths\n    expected:\n      postcondition: each row fits within 80 characters; column count is maximized\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.1\n      - prd003-format R1.4\n\n  - name: columns_empty_input\n    description: Columns returns nil for empty input.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Columns(nil, 80)\"\n    expected:\n      result: nil\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.1\n\n  - name: pad_right\n    description: PadRight pads a string with trailing spaces to the specified width.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadRight(\"abc\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"abc       \"  (abc + 7 spaces)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.2\n\n  - name: pad_left\n    description: PadLeft pads a string with leading spaces to the specified width.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadLeft(\"abc\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"       abc\"  (7 spaces + abc)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.2\n\n  - name: display_width_multibyte\n    description: Column width uses rune count, not byte count, for multi-byte strings.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'format.PadRight(\"café\", 10)'\n    expected:\n      result: '\"café      \"  (café is 4 runes, padded to 10)'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R1.3\n\n  - name: file_type_color_all_types\n    description: FileTypeColor returns correct ANSI codes for all eight file types.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(mode) for each file type\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n    expected:\n      directory: '\"\\033[34m\"'\n      symlink: '\"\\033[36m\"'\n      executable: '\"\\033[32m\"'\n      block_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n      char_device: '\"\\033[33;1m\"'\n      socket: '\"\\033[35m\"'\n      pipe: '\"\\033[33m\"'\n      regular: '\"\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.1\n      - prd003-format R2.4\n\n  - name: reset_color_enabled\n    description: Reset returns ANSI reset sequence when color is enabled.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.Reset()\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true)\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"\\033[0m\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.2\n\n  - name: color_disabled_suppresses_output\n    description: SetColorEnabled(false) causes FileTypeColor and Reset to return empty strings.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.FileTypeColor(os.ModeDir) and format.Reset()\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(false)\"\n    expected:\n      file_type_color: '\"\"'\n      reset: '\"\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.6\n\n  - name: reset_color_enabled_restores_auto\n    description: ResetColorEnabled clears the override and reverts to TTY detection.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ResetColorEnabled() then format.ColorEnabled(pipe)\"\n      setup: \"format.SetColorEnabled(true); format.ResetColorEnabled()\"\n    expected:\n      color_enabled_pipe: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.7\n\n  - name: color_enabled_pipe\n    description: ColorEnabled returns false for an os.Pipe writer.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(pipeWriter)\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.3\n\n  - name: color_enabled_non_file\n    description: ColorEnabled returns false for a bytes.Buffer (non-*os.File).\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.ColorEnabled(&bytes.Buffer{})\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R2.3\n\n  - name: human_size_binary\n    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1024-based units.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(1536, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"1.5K\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.1\n      - prd003-format R3.2\n      - prd003-format R3.3\n\n  - name: human_size_si\n    description: HumanSize converts bytes using 1000-based SI units.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(1000000, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: false})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"1.0MB\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.1\n      - prd003-format R3.2\n\n  - name: human_size_zero\n    description: HumanSize returns \"0\" for zero bytes.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"format.HumanSize(0, HumanSizeOpts{Binary: true})\"\n    expected:\n      result: '\"0\"'\n    traces:\n      - prd003-format R3.4\n\n  # --- uc003-sys: pkg/sys syscall abstractions ---\n\n  - name: terminal_width_pipe\n    description: TerminalWidth returns an error when stdout is a pipe.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.TerminalWidth() with stdout redirected to a pipe\"\n    expected:\n      error: non-nil\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R1.1\n\n  - name: is_terminal_pipe_fd\n    description: IsTerminal returns false for a pipe file descriptor.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.IsTerminal(pipeFd)\"\n    expected:\n      result: false\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R1.3\n\n  - name: stat_known_file\n    description: Stat returns correct extended metadata for a known file.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, Blocks match stat(1) output\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.1\n      - prd002-sys R2.2\n\n  - name: lstat_symlink\n    description: Lstat on a symlink returns symlink type bits, not target's mode.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.Lstat(symlinkPath)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"Mode & os.ModeSymlink != 0\"\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.1\n\n  - name: stat_modtime_populated\n    description: Stat returns a non-zero ModTime from the platform-correct field.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: ModTime is non-zero and close to os.Stat(testFile).ModTime()\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.3\n\n  - name: stat_hard_link_count\n    description: Stat returns correct Nlink for a file with multiple hard links.\n    inputs:\n      setup: \"create testFile, create hard link to testFile\"\n      function: \"sys.Stat(testFile)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: Nlink == 2\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R2.2\n\n  - name: sigpipe_handler_exit_zero\n    description: InstallSIGPIPEHandler causes exit 0 on broken pipe.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler() then write to closed pipe\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R3.1\n\n  - name: on_terminal_resize_callback\n    description: OnTerminalResize registers a callback invoked on SIGWINCH.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"sys.OnTerminalResize(callback) then send SIGWINCH\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: callback was called with a positive width\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R4.1\n      - prd002-sys R4.2\n\n  - name: cross_platform_compile\n    description: All pkg/sys code compiles on darwin/arm64 and linux/amd64.\n    inputs:\n      command: \"GOOS=darwin GOARCH=arm64 go build ./pkg/sys/ && GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 go build ./pkg/sys/\"\n    expected:\n      exit_code: 0\n    traces:\n      - prd002-sys R1.2\n\n  # --- uc004-testutils: pkg/testutils differential testing harness ---\n\n  - name: difftest_zero_value\n    description: DiffTest zero value is a valid test case that runs without error.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, echoBin, echoBin, []DiffTest{{Name: \\\"zero\\\"}})\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes with no output\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R1.1\n\n  - name: rundifftests_matching_output\n    description: RunDiffTests passes silently when both binaries produce identical output.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      setup: \"both mock binaries print \\\"hello\\\\n\\\" to stdout and exit 0\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes with no output to stdout or stderr\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.1\n      - prd001-testutils R2.4\n      - prd001-testutils R3.2\n\n  - name: rundifftests_divergent_stdout\n    description: RunDiffTests reports failure when stdout differs between binaries.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      setup: \"Go binary prints \\\"hello\\\\n\\\", reference prints \\\"world\\\\n\\\"\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"test fails with message containing args, stdin, both stdouts, both stderrs, and both exit codes\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R3.2\n      - prd001-testutils R3.5\n\n  - name: rundifftests_divergent_exit_code\n    description: RunDiffTests reports failure when exit codes differ.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\"\n      setup: \"Go binary exits 0, reference exits 1\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test fails with message showing both exit codes\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R3.4\n      - prd001-testutils R3.5\n\n  - name: timestamp_normalizer\n    description: TimestampNormalizer strips strftime timestamps so time-dependent outputs match.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Normalize: []NormalizeFunc{TimestampNormalizer}\"\n      setup: \"binaries produce outputs differing only in timestamp field\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes after normalization strips timestamps\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R4.1\n      - prd001-testutils R4.2\n\n  - name: compose_normalizers\n    description: ComposeNormalizers chains multiple functions applied in order.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.ComposeNormalizers(fn1, fn2)\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"composed function applies fn1 then fn2; output matches fn2(fn1(input))\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R4.3\n      - prd001-testutils R4.4\n\n  - name: expected_files_match\n    description: ExpectedFiles comparison passes when Go binary writes correct file content.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with ExpectedFiles\"\n      setup: \"mock binary writes expected content to output file\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test passes with no output\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R5.1\n      - prd001-testutils R5.2\n\n  - name: expected_files_diverge\n    description: ExpectedFiles comparison fails when Go binary writes wrong file content.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with ExpectedFiles\"\n      setup: \"mock binary writes different content than expected\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test fails with message showing file path, expected content, actual content\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R5.1\n      - prd001-testutils R5.2\n\n  - name: timeout_exceeded\n    description: RunDiffTests fails with timeout message when binary exceeds timeout.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with short timeout\"\n      setup: \"mock binary sleeps beyond timeout\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: test fails with clear timeout message, not a hang\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.3\n\n  - name: env_default_lc_all\n    description: RunDiffTests sets LC_ALL=C by default when DiffTest.Env is nil.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: nil\"\n      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=C\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n\n  - name: env_override_lc_all\n    description: DiffTest.Env overrides the LC_ALL=C default.\n    inputs:\n      function: 'testutils.RunDiffTests with Env: []string{\"LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"}'\n      setup: \"mock binary prints LC_ALL environment variable\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: \"binary receives LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\"\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R1.3\n      - prd001-testutils R2.6\n\n  - name: workdir_default_tempdir\n    description: WorkDir defaults to t.TempDir() when empty.\n    inputs:\n      function: \"testutils.RunDiffTests with WorkDir: \\\"\\\"\"\n      setup: \"mock binary prints working directory\"\n    expected:\n      postcondition: both binaries run in a temporary directory\n    traces:\n      - prd001-testutils R2.5\n","numLines":493,"startLine":1,"totalLines":493}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MNjV6STC4DXarWSZ4nWgUe","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: prd001-testutils\n     2→title: \"pkg/testutils: Differential Testing Harness\"\n     3→\n     4→problem: |\n     5→  Every utility in go-unix-utils is verified by running the Go binary and the Homebrew\n     6→  GNU reference binary side by side and comparing their stdout, stderr, and exit code.\n     7→  Without a shared harness, each cmd/ package would duplicate the execution and comparison\n     8→  logic, the normalization hooks needed for non-deterministic output (timestamps in ts,\n     9→  path ordering in find), and the divergence reporting format. This duplication makes\n    10→  the verification layer fragile: a bug in one cmd/'s harness copy would produce\n    11→  different verification behavior than another cmd/'s copy.\n    12→\n    13→  pkg/testutils is the acceptance gate for the entire pipeline. The cobbler orchestrator\n    14→  cannot declare a utility complete until its differential tests pass through this harness.\n    15→  This PRD is also the authoritative API reference for stitch agents implementing cmd/\n    16→  packages: the agent reads this document, knows the full pkg/testutils API, and imports\n    17→  the package without reinventing it.\n    18→\n    19→  A cmd/ test file imports pkg/testutils and defines test cases as data. The stitch agent\n    20→  producing a new cmd/ utility writes only the test file — it does not recreate the package.\n    21→  The canonical usage pattern is:\n    22→\n    23→    package main_test\n    24→\n    25→    import (\n    26→        \"os\"\n    27→        \"testing\"\n    28→        \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n    29→    )\n    30→\n    31→    func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n    32→        goBin := os.Getenv(\"GO_BINARY\")\n    33→        refBin := os.Getenv(\"REF_BINARY\")\n    34→        tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n    35→            {Name: \"basic\", Args: []string{\"-n\", \"testdata/input.txt\"}, ExitCode: 0},\n    36→            {Name: \"stdin\", Args: []string{\"-c\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"hello\\n\"), ExitCode: 0},\n    37→            {Name: \"normalized\", Args: []string{\"-s\", \"%H:%M:%S\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"event\\n\"),\n    38→                ExitCode: 0, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{testutils.TimestampNormalizer}},\n    39→        }\n    40→        testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n    41→    }\n    42→\n    43→goals:\n    44→  - G1: Provide a single execution function that runs a Go binary and a GNU reference binary with identical inputs and returns both outputs for comparison.\n    45→  - G2: Provide a comparison function that diffs stdout, stderr, and exit code and reports divergence with the triggering input.\n    46→  - G3: Provide a normalization hook mechanism so individual utilities can strip or replace non-deterministic output fields before comparison.\n    47→  - G4: Integrate with go test so that each cmd/ package can define test cases as data and call the harness from a standard TestXxx function.\n    48→\n    49→requirements:\n    50→  R1:\n    51→    title: Test case data structure\n    52→    items:\n    53→      - R1.1: |\n    54→          Must define DiffTest as the following named struct in package testutils:\n    55→\n    56→            type DiffTest struct {\n    57→                Name          string                 // subtest name used with t.Run; required\n    58→                Args          []string               // command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n    59→                Stdin         []byte                 // nil = no stdin (both binaries receive EOF immediately)\n    60→                Env           []string               // nil = use defaults only (LC_ALL=C); non-nil = KEY=VALUE pairs merged into inherited environment\n    61→                WorkDir       string                 // empty = per-test t.TempDir(); non-empty = use this directory for both binaries\n    62→                ExitCode      int                    // expected exit code for both binaries\n    63→                Normalize     []func([]byte) []byte  // applied in order to stdout and stderr of both binaries before comparison; nil or empty = no normalization\n    64→                ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte      // optional: path -> expected byte content after execution, for file-output utilities (sponge, cp)\n    65→            }\n    66→      - R1.2: DiffTest.Stdin nil means both binaries receive EOF immediately on stdin. An empty non-nil slice ([]byte{}) also produces no bytes but is semantically distinct (open stdin that is immediately closed).\n    67→      - R1.3: |\n    68→          DiffTest.Env nil means both binaries inherit the test process environment with\n    69→          default overrides applied (see R2.6). When non-nil, the KEY=VALUE pairs in the\n    70→          slice are merged into the inherited environment: matching keys are overridden, new\n    71→          keys are added. This merge behavior matches the struct comment (\"override or\n    72→          extend\") and avoids requiring callers to replicate the full environment for a\n    73→          single override.\n    74→      - R1.4: Must define type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte as a named type alias in package testutils. The Normalize field in DiffTest uses this element type. When the slice is nil or empty, no normalization is applied to stdout or stderr.\n    75→\n    76→  R2:\n    77→    title: Binary execution\n    78→    items:\n    79→      - R2.1: |\n    80→          Must provide func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) that accepts the path to the Go binary under test (goBinary) and the GNU reference binary (refBinary), then runs each DiffTest as a named subtest via t.Run(test.Name, ...). Both binaries are invoked with identical Args, Stdin, and Env for each test case.\n    81→      - R2.2: Must capture stdout, stderr, and exit code from each binary independently.\n    82→      - R2.3: Must impose a configurable timeout on each binary invocation. The default timeout must be 10 seconds. The test fails if either binary exceeds the timeout.\n    83→      - R2.4: Must not write any output to the test process stdout or stderr during a passing test run.\n    84→      - R2.5: |\n    85→          Must support passing a working directory to each binary invocation via a WorkDir\n    86→          field on DiffTest. When WorkDir is empty, both binaries run in a per-test temporary\n    87→          directory created by the harness via t.TempDir(). The harness must use the same\n    88→          working directory for both binaries in a given test case. The DiffTest struct gains:\n    89→\n    90→            WorkDir string // empty = per-test t.TempDir(); non-empty = use this directory for both binaries\n    91→      - R2.6: |\n    92→          Must set LC_ALL=C in the environment for both binaries unless the DiffTest.Env\n    93→          explicitly overrides LC_ALL. This ensures deterministic sort order and formatting\n    94→          across locales. The harness applies this default before merging DiffTest.Env.\n    95→\n    96→  R3:\n    97→    title: Comparison and reporting\n    98→    items:\n    99→      - R3.1: Must apply the DiffTest.Normalize function (if non-nil) to both binaries' stdout and stderr before comparison.\n   100→      - R3.2: Must compare normalized stdout byte-for-byte. Any difference must be reported as a test failure.\n   101→      - R3.3: Must compare normalized stderr byte-for-byte. Any difference must be reported as a test failure.\n   102→      - R3.4: Must compare exit codes exactly. A difference must be reported as a test failure.\n   103→      - R3.5: 'Must report divergence with the following information in the failure message: the DiffTest args, the stdin content (truncated to 256 bytes if longer), the reference binary stdout, the Go binary stdout, the reference stderr, the Go stderr, and both exit codes.'\n   104→      - R3.6: Must run each DiffTest as a named subtest (t.Run) so individual test case failures are identifiable in go test output.\n   105→\n   106→  R4:\n   107→    title: Normalization hooks\n   108→    items:\n   109→      - R4.1: Must allow per-DiffTest normalization via the Normalize field. The function receives the raw output bytes and returns the normalized bytes.\n   110→      - R4.2: Must provide a built-in TimestampNormalizer that replaces common strftime timestamp patterns with a fixed placeholder string. This normalizer is used by cmd/ts tests.\n   111→      - R4.3: |\n   112→          Must allow normalizers to be composed: the harness must accept a slice of Normalize\n   113→          functions applied in order, not a single function. When the slice is nil or empty,\n   114→          no normalization is applied.\n   115→      - R4.4: |\n   116→          Must provide func ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc that returns\n   117→          a single NormalizeFunc applying the given functions in order. This is a convenience\n   118→          for cmd/ test files that combine multiple normalizers:\n   119→\n   120→            normalize := testutils.ComposeNormalizers(\n   121→                testutils.TimestampNormalizer,\n   122→                customNormalizer,\n   123→            )\n   124→\n   125→  R5:\n   126→    title: File-state comparison\n   127→    items:\n   128→      - R5.1: |\n   129→          Must support utilities whose primary output is a file rather than stdout (sponge,\n   130→          cp, mv). DiffTest.ExpectedFiles is a map[string][]byte where keys are file paths\n   131→          relative to the working directory and values are the expected byte content after\n   132→          execution. When ExpectedFiles is non-nil, the harness checks each entry after both\n   133→          binaries complete.\n   134→      - R5.2: |\n   135→          Must compare each ExpectedFiles entry byte-for-byte against the file produced by\n   136→          the Go binary. Any difference must be reported as a test failure with the same\n   137→          format as stdout divergence: file path, expected content (from reference), actual\n   138→          content (from Go binary). Missing files must also be reported as failures.\n   139→\n   140→non_goals:\n   141→  - pkg/testutils does not build or compile the Go binaries under test.\n   142→  - pkg/testutils does not install or manage Homebrew reference binaries.\n   143→  - pkg/testutils does not produce test reports beyond standard go test output.\n   144→  - pkg/testutils does not implement retry logic; a failing test fails immediately.\n   145→  - pkg/testutils does not mock or stub the filesystem or OS for unit testing cmd/ packages.\n   146→\n   147→acceptance_criteria:\n   148→  - \"AC1: A cmd/ package can define a []DiffTest slice and call RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) from a TestXxx function with no other setup. RunDiffTests runs each DiffTest as a named subtest (t.Run(test.Name, ...)) and calls t.Fatal on the first divergence in any subtest.\"\n   149→  - \"AC2: A passing test run produces no output. A failing test prints the triggering args, stdin, and both binaries' stdout, stderr, and exit code.\"\n   150→  - \"AC3: TimestampNormalizer replaces strftime-formatted timestamps (e.g., \\\"Feb 19 12:34:56\\\") with a fixed placeholder so that ts differential tests pass despite wall-clock differences.\"\n   151→  - \"AC4: A DiffTest with ExpectedFiles correctly fails when the Go binary writes different file content than expected.\"\n   152→  - \"AC5: A DiffTest that exceeds the timeout fails with a clear timeout message rather than hanging the test run.\"\n   153→  - \"AC6: All pkg/testutils code compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n   154→  - \"AC7: ComposeNormalizers combines multiple NormalizeFunc values into a single function that applies them in order.\"\n   155→  - \"AC8: RunDiffTests sets LC_ALL=C by default. A DiffTest with Env=[\\\"LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\\\"] overrides this default.\"\n   156→  - \"AC9: The usage example in the problem statement is sufficient for a stitch agent to write a cmd/ test file that imports pkg/testutils without recreating the package.\"\n   157→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1b79863-0b40-4bd6-8be0-3edd1f9e69f7","uuid":"baf000f2-0066-4e4d-ad46-b1e488b7406c","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/86/docs/specs/product-requirements/prd001-testutils.yaml","content":"id: prd001-testutils\ntitle: \"pkg/testutils: Differential Testing Harness\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Every utility in go-unix-utils is verified by running the Go binary and the Homebrew\n  GNU reference binary side by side and comparing their stdout, stderr, and exit code.\n  Without a shared harness, each cmd/ package would duplicate the execution and comparison\n  logic, the normalization hooks needed for non-deterministic output (timestamps in ts,\n  path ordering in find), and the divergence reporting format. This duplication makes\n  the verification layer fragile: a bug in one cmd/'s harness copy would produce\n  different verification behavior than another cmd/'s copy.\n\n  pkg/testutils is the acceptance gate for the entire pipeline. The cobbler orchestrator\n  cannot declare a utility complete until its differential tests pass through this harness.\n  This PRD is also the authoritative API reference for stitch agents implementing cmd/\n  packages: the agent reads this document, knows the full pkg/testutils API, and imports\n  the package without reinventing it.\n\n  A cmd/ test file imports pkg/testutils and defines test cases as data. The stitch agent\n  producing a new cmd/ utility writes only the test file — it does not recreate the package.\n  The canonical usage pattern is:\n\n    package main_test\n\n    import (\n        \"os\"\n        \"testing\"\n        \"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/testutils\"\n    )\n\n    func TestDiff(t *testing.T) {\n        goBin := os.Getenv(\"GO_BINARY\")\n        refBin := os.Getenv(\"REF_BINARY\")\n        tests := []testutils.DiffTest{\n            {Name: \"basic\", Args: []string{\"-n\", \"testdata/input.txt\"}, ExitCode: 0},\n            {Name: \"stdin\", Args: []string{\"-c\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"hello\\n\"), ExitCode: 0},\n            {Name: \"normalized\", Args: []string{\"-s\", \"%H:%M:%S\"}, Stdin: []byte(\"event\\n\"),\n                ExitCode: 0, Normalize: []testutils.NormalizeFunc{testutils.TimestampNormalizer}},\n        }\n        testutils.RunDiffTests(t, goBin, refBin, tests)\n    }\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Provide a single execution function that runs a Go binary and a GNU reference binary with identical inputs and returns both outputs for comparison.\n  - G2: Provide a comparison function that diffs stdout, stderr, and exit code and reports divergence with the triggering input.\n  - G3: Provide a normalization hook mechanism so individual utilities can strip or replace non-deterministic output fields before comparison.\n  - G4: Integrate with go test so that each cmd/ package can define test cases as data and call the harness from a standard TestXxx function.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Test case data structure\n    items:\n      - R1.1: |\n          Must define DiffTest as the following named struct in package testutils:\n\n            type DiffTest struct {\n                Name          string                 // subtest name used with t.Run; required\n                Args          []string               // command-line arguments passed to both binaries\n                Stdin         []byte                 // nil = no stdin (both binaries receive EOF immediately)\n                Env           []string               // nil = use defaults only (LC_ALL=C); non-nil = KEY=VALUE pairs merged into inherited environment\n                WorkDir       string                 // empty = per-test t.TempDir(); non-empty = use this directory for both binaries\n                ExitCode      int                    // expected exit code for both binaries\n                Normalize     []func([]byte) []byte  // applied in order to stdout and stderr of both binaries before comparison; nil or empty = no normalization\n                ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte      // optional: path -> expected byte content after execution, for file-output utilities (sponge, cp)\n            }\n      - R1.2: DiffTest.Stdin nil means both binaries receive EOF immediately on stdin. An empty non-nil slice ([]byte{}) also produces no bytes but is semantically distinct (open stdin that is immediately closed).\n      - R1.3: |\n          DiffTest.Env nil means both binaries inherit the test process environment with\n          default overrides applied (see R2.6). When non-nil, the KEY=VALUE pairs in the\n          slice are merged into the inherited environment: matching keys are overridden, new\n          keys are added. This merge behavior matches the struct comment (\"override or\n          extend\") and avoids requiring callers to replicate the full environment for a\n          single override.\n      - R1.4: Must define type NormalizeFunc = func([]byte) []byte as a named type alias in package testutils. The Normalize field in DiffTest uses this element type. When the slice is nil or empty, no normalization is applied to stdout or stderr.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Binary execution\n    items:\n      - R2.1: |\n          Must provide func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) that accepts the path to the Go binary under test (goBinary) and the GNU reference binary (refBinary), then runs each DiffTest as a named subtest via t.Run(test.Name, ...). Both binaries are invoked with identical Args, Stdin, and Env for each test case.\n      - R2.2: Must capture stdout, stderr, and exit code from each binary independently.\n      - R2.3: Must impose a configurable timeout on each binary invocation. The default timeout must be 10 seconds. The test fails if either binary exceeds the timeout.\n      - R2.4: Must not write any output to the test process stdout or stderr during a passing test run.\n      - R2.5: |\n          Must support passing a working directory to each binary invocation via a WorkDir\n          field on DiffTest. When WorkDir is empty, both binaries run in a per-test temporary\n          directory created by the harness via t.TempDir(). The harness must use the same\n          working directory for both binaries in a given test case. The DiffTest struct gains:\n\n            WorkDir string // empty = per-test t.TempDir(); non-empty = use this directory for both binaries\n      - R2.6: |\n          Must set LC_ALL=C in the environment for both binaries unless the DiffTest.Env\n          explicitly overrides LC_ALL. This ensures deterministic sort order and formatting\n          across locales. The harness applies this default before merging DiffTest.Env.\n\n  R3:\n    title: Comparison and reporting\n    items:\n      - R3.1: Must apply the DiffTest.Normalize function (if non-nil) to both binaries' stdout and stderr before comparison.\n      - R3.2: Must compare normalized stdout byte-for-byte. Any difference must be reported as a test failure.\n      - R3.3: Must compare normalized stderr byte-for-byte. Any difference must be reported as a test failure.\n      - R3.4: Must compare exit codes exactly. A difference must be reported as a test failure.\n      - R3.5: 'Must report divergence with the following information in the failure message: the DiffTest args, the stdin content (truncated to 256 bytes if longer), the reference binary stdout, the Go binary stdout, the reference stderr, the Go stderr, and both exit codes.'\n      - R3.6: Must run each DiffTest as a named subtest (t.Run) so individual test case failures are identifiable in go test output.\n\n  R4:\n    title: Normalization hooks\n    items:\n      - R4.1: Must allow per-DiffTest normalization via the Normalize field. The function receives the raw output bytes and returns the normalized bytes.\n      - R4.2: Must provide a built-in TimestampNormalizer that replaces common strftime timestamp patterns with a fixed placeholder string. This normalizer is used by cmd/ts tests.\n      - R4.3: |\n          Must allow normalizers to be composed: the harness must accept a slice of Normalize\n          functions applied in order, not a single function. When the slice is nil or empty,\n          no normalization is applied.\n      - R4.4: |\n          Must provide func ComposeNormalizers(fns ...NormalizeFunc) NormalizeFunc that returns\n          a single NormalizeFunc applying the given functions in order. This is a convenience\n          for cmd/ test files that combine multiple normalizers:\n\n            normalize := testutils.ComposeNormalizers(\n                testutils.TimestampNormalizer,\n                customNormalizer,\n            )\n\n  R5:\n    title: File-state comparison\n    items:\n      - R5.1: |\n          Must support utilities whose primary output is a file rather than stdout (sponge,\n          cp, mv). DiffTest.ExpectedFiles is a map[string][]byte where keys are file paths\n          relative to the working directory and values are the expected byte content after\n          execution. When ExpectedFiles is non-nil, the harness checks each entry after both\n          binaries complete.\n      - R5.2: |\n          Must compare each ExpectedFiles entry byte-for-byte against the file produced by\n          the Go binary. Any difference must be reported as a test failure with the same\n          format as stdout divergence: file path, expected content (from reference), actual\n          content (from Go binary). Missing files must also be reported as failures.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - pkg/testutils does not build or compile the Go binaries under test.\n  - pkg/testutils does not install or manage Homebrew reference binaries.\n  - pkg/testutils does not produce test reports beyond standard go test output.\n  - pkg/testutils does not implement retry logic; a failing test fails immediately.\n  - pkg/testutils does not mock or stub the filesystem or OS for unit testing cmd/ packages.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - \"AC1: A cmd/ package can define a []DiffTest slice and call RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest) from a TestXxx function with no other setup. RunDiffTests runs each DiffTest as a named subtest (t.Run(test.Name, ...)) and calls t.Fatal on the first divergence in any subtest.\"\n  - \"AC2: A passing test run produces no output. A failing test prints the triggering args, stdin, and both binaries' stdout, stderr, and exit code.\"\n  - \"AC3: TimestampNormalizer replaces strftime-formatted timestamps (e.g., \\\"Feb 19 12:34:56\\\") with a fixed placeholder so that ts differential tests pass despite wall-clock differences.\"\n  - \"AC4: A DiffTest with ExpectedFiles correctly fails when the Go binary writes different file content than expected.\"\n  - \"AC5: A DiffTest that exceeds the timeout fails with a clear timeout message rather than hanging the test run.\"\n  - \"AC6: All pkg/testutils code compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n  - \"AC7: ComposeNormalizers combines multiple NormalizeFunc values into a single function that applies them in order.\"\n  - \"AC8: RunDiffTests sets LC_ALL=C by default. A DiffTest with Env=[\\\"LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8\\\"] overrides this default.\"\n  - \"AC9: The usage example in the problem statement is sufficient for a stitch agent to write a cmd/ test file that imports pkg/testutils without recreating the package.\"\n","numLines":157,"startLine":1,"totalLines":157}}}
